Middleware runs in registration order before handlers, can write to req.ctx,
can be scoped with ON "/path/*", and stops the handler when it calls RESPOND
or throws (Requirement 8.1, 8.2).

### global middleware runs in order; scoped middleware is skipped on /public
GET /public
=> 200

{"order": ["first", "second"], "admin": null}

### scoped middleware runs on /admin/* and passes through
GET /admin/vault
X-Pass: ok

=> 200

{"order": ["first", "second"], "admin": true}

### middleware RESPOND stops the handler
GET /admin/vault
X-Pass: deny

=> 403

{"error": "FORBIDDEN BY THE CRYPT"}

### middleware THROW stops the handler
GET /admin/vault
X-Pass: throw

=> 401

{"error": "NO PASS PROVIDED"}
